    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d895">

                <pb facs="1109" n="1099" xml:id="pg1099"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–1647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-16T23:00:00+03:00">April 16, 1947—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 17—6:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1407. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kosmos</hi> 44. For Acheson from Marshall.
                    Please reply to Stuart’s 801 in sense of your <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Moskco</hi> 60 and indicate my concurrence.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d895-f1"
                    /> [Marshall.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d895-f1" n="35" xml:id="d895-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 445, April 17, 6 p.m., the Acting Secretary complied with this
                    instruction by repeating to the Ambassador in China this telegram and
                    Department’s telegram No. 924 (<hi rendition="#small-caps">Moskco</hi> 60), <ref
                        target="#pg1097">p. 1097</ref>. (893.00/4–1247)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
